<circuit version="1.1.0-SR2" rev="261103" stepSize="1000000" stepsPS="1000000" NLsteps="100000" reaStep="1000000" animate="0" >
<description>
# MT7833A: inside of the part

Drawn like the block diagram on datasheet p.4. The tunnels named like the package pins (VDD, GND, DSEN, CS, COMP, D5/D6 = DRAIN) are the IC's pins; EN and GATE are internal.

- **Supply &amp; VDD detection, Start-up** (`SUP`, script): start at 18 V, lockout at 9 V, supply current through `IVDD` (link 0), 24 V clamp `ZVDD`. Drives **EN** (`VEN`, link 1). A FAULT starts the hiccup.
- **Feedback detection** (`FB`, script): samples DSEN 2 µs after each turn-off; **ZCD** when demagnetised (`VZCD`), **FAULT** on OVP or SCP (`VFAULT`).
- **PWM controller** (`PWM`, script): on-time from COMP, off on OCP, on again at ZCD (≥ 10 µs); drives the **Driver** `VGATE` (link 0) holds the average of CS over the last cycle on `VISENSE` (link 1, loaded by `R_IS`) and computes the **EA**: current `VEA` (link 2) into COMP.
- **OCP**: op-amp, CS &gt; 1.4 V (`VOCP`). **EA**: gm 200 µS × (0.2 V − ISENSE), ± 59 µA into COMP; `R_EA` (85 kΩ) pre-charges and discharges COMP.

Every signal is relative to GND, so the IC ground may float. Not a circuit to run on its own: place the part from the component list (Projects / Power ICs). See `components/MT7833A/README.md`.
</description>


